{
	"$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
	"$id": "flauz.orch.protocol/v1",
	"title": "Flauz orchestration service protocol contract (flauz.orch/v1)",
	"description": "The message shapes between the extension layer and the Flauz orchestration service (TL2-001 M4). This schema is the versioned JSON contract document; core/orchProtocol.mjs is the typed executable mirror (validators + registry) and the conformance suite pins the two bidirectionally (method/event/failure enums and the per-method required/optional key lists must agree exactly). The protocol rides the TL1-003 service seam (flauz.seam/v1) for transport: hello/ready handshake, {id, cmd, args} request framing, structured flauz.err.* error envelopes and {type: event, event, payload, ts} wire events - never duplicated here. Approval expiry (flauz.orch.expireApproval / orch-approval-expired) arrives with the TL2-004 closure as additive v1 growth.",
